# Year 7 English Language Lesson Topics

This document contains proposed curriculum topics for Year 7 (KS3 / Grade 6–7) English Language, designed with interactive components in mind.

---

## Topic 1: 🦸‍♂️ The Art of Hero & Villain Creation (Descriptive Writing)
* **Core Skills**: Characterization, sensory details, vivid verbs, figurative language (metaphors, similes, personification).
* **Overview**: Students design opposing characters (a superhero and a supervillain), write contrasting entry scenes, and learn how word choices evoke empathy vs. tension.
* **Suggested Interactive Components**:
  * Matching pairs: Figurative language definitions vs. character descriptions
  * Fill-in-the-blanks: Descriptive adjectives & sensory words in hero/villain passages
  * Flashcards: Analyzing character traits and archetype tropes

---

## Topic 2: 🕵️‍♂️ Mystery & Suspense: Crafting Atmosphere (Creative Writing)
* **Core Skills**: Building tension, pacing, "show, don't tell", sentence structure variation (short impact vs. long descriptive sentences).
* **Overview**: Explores classic mystery tropes (haunted rooms, hidden doors, mysterious sounds) and teaches how to manipulate mood to keep a reader hooked.
* **Suggested Interactive Components**:
  * Hotspot: Finding sensory details in a spooky scene image
  * Drag-and-drop: Sorting sentences into "Tension Building" vs. "Atmosphere Setting"
  * Quiz: Identifying "Show, Don't Tell" techniques

---

## Topic 3: 📢 Persuasive Power & Advertising Myths (Rhetoric & Argumentation)
* **Core Skills**: Persuasive techniques (AFOREST: Alliteration, Facts, Opinion, Rhetorical questions, Emotive language, Statistics, Rule of Three).
* **Overview**: Students analyze real-world advertisements, spot manipulative techniques, and pitch an impossible product using persuasive writing.
* **Suggested Interactive Components**:
  * Flashcards: AFOREST acronym breakdown & examples
  * Drag-and-drop: Classifying statements into Fact vs. Opinion vs. Emotive Language
  * Quiz: Spotting persuasive techniques in sample advert slogans

---

## Topic 4: 📰 Fake News vs. Real Headlines (Media Literacy & Non-Fiction)
* **Core Skills**: Bias, tone, formal vs. informal register, headline conventions, objective vs. subjective reporting.
* **Overview**: Students compare tabloid vs. broadsheet coverage of the same event, spot sensationalism, and write their own balanced news report.
* **Suggested Interactive Components**:
  * Matching pairs: Headline types (Sensational vs. Objective)
  * Fill-in-the-blanks: Register transformation (Informal → Formal news report)
  * Quiz: Identifying media bias in news excerpts

---

## Topic 5: 🌍 Mythology & Legend Rewrites (Narrative Structure & Mythmaking)
* **Core Skills**: Narrative arc (exposition, rising action, climax, resolution), dialogue punctuation, archetype development.
* **Overview**: Draws on Greek, Norse, or African myths, analyzing what makes them timeless, and guides students to re-imagine a classic myth in a modern or sci-fi setting.
* **Suggested Interactive Components**:
  * Drag-and-drop: Ordering the stages of the Hero's Journey / Narrative Arc
  * Flashcards: Mythological archetypes (The Hero, The Trickster, The Mentor)
  * Matching pairs: Punctuating dialogue correctly in myth excerpts
